  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let \\(y=e^{-x} \\cos x\\)\n\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{y}_1=-e^{-x} \\sin x-e^{-x} \\cos x=-e^{-x} \\sin x-y \\\\\n& y_2=-e^{-x} \\cos x+e^{-x} \\sin x-y_1 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow y_2=-y-y_1+e^{-x} \\sin x=-2\\left(y+y_1\\right) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow y_3=-2\\left(y_1+y_2\\right)=-2\\left(e^{-x} \\sin x-y\\right) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow y_4=4 y_1+2 y_2=4 y_1-4 y-4 y_1 \\text { or } y_4+4 y=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow k=4\n\\end{aligned}\\)",
    "image": null
  },
